\DOC ENSURES_INIT_TAC

\TYPE {ENSURES_INIT_TAC : string -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Converts an {ensures}-style Hoare-triple goal into an {eventually} goal about a
named initial state, moving the precondition into the assumptions.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {sname : string} names the universally quantified initial state
variable (call it {s}), which becomes the state appearing in the new
assumptions and in the resulting {eventually} goal. Applied to a goal whose
conclusion is an {ensures} triple, the tactic instantiates the precondition {P}
at {s}, splits the instantiated precondition along its conjunctions —
descending through nested parenthesised conjuncts — and adds each resulting
conjunct as a separate assumption; the component terms are otherwise unchanged,
so a conjunct that is not itself a conjunction, such as an implication or an
existential, is added whole. It also adds a reflexivity-style assumption saying
that the empty frame relates {s} to itself. The pre-existing assumptions {A}
are all retained, in order, ahead of the new ones. In the conclusion, the
postcondition body and the frame {C} are conjoined under a fresh bound state
variable.
{
       A ?- ensures step P Q C
   =========================================================  ENSURES_INIT_TAC sname
       A, p1, ..., pn, (empty frame relates s to s)
         ?- eventually step (\s'. Q s' /\ C s s') s
}
\noindent where {p1 ... pn} are the conjuncts of {P s}.

\COMMENTS
Every observed trace shows this single kind of transformation, applied to goals
whose conclusion is an {ensures} triple.

\ENDDOC
